dotNumT -- F-117 ON THE OLD ROAD (Tony's ruling (a), 2026-09-24): A NUMBER NEEDS A LEADING DIGIT. `.5` is refused by
name -- REFUSED ... `.5` is not a number ... write 0.5 -- and its print statement prints nothing; `print 0.5;` is the
control and prints 0.5. Before the ruling the old road read `.5` as a leading-dot accessor with no target and died
in opDot at exit 139. The new-road twin is unaryNatT's unPrDot and unPr05 copies.
